cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RASP5, cite this software and the original papers for every analysis engine and model used."
title: "RASP5: an auditable desktop workbench for historical biogeography and ancestral trait reconstruction"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Xu
    given-names: Yan
repository-code: "https://github.com/Yxu-bio/RASP_test"
url: "https://github.com/Yxu-bio/RASP_test"
version: "5.0.0-dev.0"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - historical biogeography
  - ancestral state reconstruction
  - BioGeoBEARS
  - stochastic mapping
  - phylogenetics
abstract: >-
  RASP5 connects phylogenetic trees, geographic range and trait matrices,
  spatial records, established reconstruction engines, normalized ancestral
  results, and stochastic biogeographic event summaries in a Windows desktop
  workflow.
